OpenDuet patch for CopilotKit/OpenBot agent-computer (MIT) at da9a3caf5784074baa779110dd7e9d1338c8871b.
/files/write no longer waits for a person to hand the browser back (it reaches only /workspace); /exec still does.
Applied in /app by computer/Dockerfile: patch -p1 --forward --fuzz=0. Regenerated with diff -ruN.

diff -ruN a/src/authorisation.ts b/src/authorisation.ts
--- a/src/authorisation.ts	2026-10-28 00:00:00
+++ b/src/authorisation.ts	2026-10-28 00:00:00
@@ -64,6 +64,11 @@
  * Reading is not acting. `/files/read` and `/files/list` stay open so a Bot that has been stopped can
  * still read its own notes and explain what it was doing, which is the answer the person handing the
  * wheel back usually wants.
+ *
+ * OpenDuet patch 0005: `/files/write` is not acting either. It writes inside /workspace through the
+ * same confinement as reading and reaches neither the browser nor its profile (/profiles), so a Make
+ * build saving its page no longer waits for a person who took the browser and forgot to hand it
+ * back. `/exec` stays on the list: a shell can reach the browser's processes and profile.
  */
 const ACTING_PATHS = new Set([
   "/navigate",
@@ -72,7 +77,6 @@
   "/key",
   "/scroll",
   "/exec",
-  "/files/write",
   // Typing a person's login into the page. Refused while they hold the wheel, like any other typing.
   "/sign-in/fill",
   "/sign-in/code",
